// expect: 6
// A `|>` chain inside an interpolation splice renders the wrong value: the
// splice below should be "(a, b)", six bytes, and it renders an ADDRESS. The
// pipe's own node judges String; the show reads its operand's type through the
// LOWERED operand's handle, and a hole-completing pipe lowers to the call it
// completes, whose node is the partial application — a function, so the show
// takes the word floor and prints a pointer. The same join spelled directly
// (`join(sep(), xs)`) or behind a named fn renders right. Measured 2026-09-23,
// also on the boot before patterns became nodes; found when a formatter
// render wrote `Sample(99972)`. Declared RED until the show reads the node it
// shows (Hβ.lower.pipe-completion-carries-the-stage-handle).
fn sep() = ", "

fn main() = len("({["a", "b"] |> join(sep())})")
